										"$class": "/Game/Blueprints/MissionSystem/Objects/Terminal/Sequences/BP_TerminalSequence_Text.BP_TerminalSequence_Text_C",
										"Widget": "/Game/Blueprints/MissionSystem/UI/Terminal/Response/W_TerminalResponse_Text.W_TerminalResponse_Text_C",
										"Events": [],
										"Text": {
											"$text": "# UICS FORWARD NODE OSK-3 – README\r\n\r\nYou are connected to Forward Node OSK-3, the UICS terminal serving the Outskirts Security Cordon (Sector 12, city perimeter).\r\n\r\nThis node coordinates checkpoint traffic, fuel and ration distribution, and patrol rotations between the rail yard, the water treatment plant and the residential blocks east of the ring road.\r\n\r\n## SYSTEM FUNCTIONS\r\n\r\n- **read** – Open and view a file's contents\r\n- **run** – Execute a terminal-compatible program\r\n- **scan** – Check a file for classification markers or hidden data\r\n- **download** – Copy a file from the node to your local device\r\n\r\nUse `help` at any time for the full command list.\r\n\r\n## CLEARANCE LEVELS\r\n\r\n- Guest: Bulletins and public notices only\r\n- Quartermaster: Logistics, fuel and supply records\r\n- Admin: Cordon command, patrol orders and node configuration\r\n\r\n## STANDING ORDERS\r\n\r\n- Credentials are personal. Rotations are logged against the account that issued them.\r\n- Encrypted intercept volumes open only with a matching Defense intel key. Do not attempt to brute-force them; the node reports every attempt to Sector Command.\r\n- If the node is compromised, run a full shutdown and fall back to Checkpoint Bravo.\r\n\r\nUICS — Order. Stability. Control.\r\n\r\n> END OF FILE"
										}
									}
								]
							}
						}
					},
